  {
   "key": "DATA-212",
   "fields": {
    "summary": "Billing v3 invoice amounts look 100x too small for 2016 - Q1 2017",
    "status": {
     "name": "Won't Do"
    },
    "created": "2017-06-02T14:11:09.000+0000",
    "description": "Revenue dashboard shows Jan 2016 at ~1% of what finance has. Investigating.",
    "comment": {
     "comments": [
      {
       "author": {
        "displayName": "Yuki Tanaka"
       },
       "created": "2017-06-05T10:02:44.000+0000",
       "body": "Root cause: the ledger import (metadata.source = ledger_import_2017) wrote subtotal/amount_due in DOLLARS with 2 decimals. Everything created natively in billing v3 is in CENTS (integer). Data dictionary says cents for all rows - it is wrong for the imported ones."
      },
      {
       "author": {
        "displayName": "Femi Adeyemi"
       },
       "created": "2017-06-05T16:40:00.000+0000",
       "body": "Can we just rewrite them? Finance doesn't want history touched after close."
      },
      {
       "author": {
        "displayName": "Ines Delacroix"
       },
       "created": "2017-06-06T09:15:12.000+0000",
       "body": "Correct - do not modify. Downstream: if source = ledger_import_2017 treat as dollars. Also note those invoices ALSO exist in the Ledger dump, don't double count."
      }
     ]
    }
   }
